[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FHI-54
TITLE: QC Read - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
Verify the single-diode analog QC acquisition lifecycle, wire-channel mapping, DMA half-boundary
stop behavior, and error reporting.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. The system, QC collimator, main-control board, and head-interface board are connected.
2. PC2 (``ADC1_IN12``) can be driven with a known voltage within the ADC input range.
3. TIM2 update triggers and DMA2 Stream 0 timing can be observed, and an ADC or DMA fault can be
   injected.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Confirm idle PC2 monitoring, then command Accumulating and wait for Active.
2. Hold PC2 at a known ADC code through at least one complete 32-sample DMA burst.
3. Command Stopped before half-transfer in one run and after half-transfer in a second run.
4. Repeat acquisition while injecting an ADC or DMA error.
5. Read the head-interface report after each transition.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Temperature and pressure monitoring stop before TIM2-triggered ADC1 DMA sampling begins, and
   only ADC1 DMA2 Stream 0 callbacks affect QC acquisition.
2. PC2 values accumulate only in wire channel 0; each full burst adds 32 samples. Wire channel 1
   remains at zero samples, zero accumulation, and disconnected.
3. Stop before half-transfer adds no samples from that burst. Stop after half-transfer preserves
   exactly the first 16 conversions and completes after the second 16 conversions.
4. No DMA half is counted twice. The report contains both wire-channel sums, both counts, and a
   coherent Active, Complete, or Error state.
5. An injected error invalidates the active transfer, reports Error, preserves committed data only,
   and restores the software-triggered ADC1 monitoring sequence.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FHI-53
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FHI-56
TITLE: Robot Hand Guidance Button Test - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
Service user should verify that the robot arm moves in manually guided positions when the button is pressed down and holds its position
upon release.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. The user should be service user
2. The system should be powered on
3. The robot arm should be ready and in a safe, reachable position to move
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Check the system is powered on
2. Check the robot status LED and robot controller to ensure arm is ready for hand guidance
3. If the button is not safely reachable, use the GUI to change the arm to the “Treatment” position
4. With one hand holding the opposite side of the treatment hand, and the other holding the bar with the manual guidance button, press and hold the button down
5. Gently push the robot arm in all 6 directions: forward, backward, left, right, up, and down, within comfortable reach
6. Release the robot hand guidance button
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. The system should appear in normal operation with no interlocks or errors tripped.
2. The system should be on, and the robot arm LED should be flashing blue
3. The robot arm moves to the treatment position with no issues. The head can be reached.
4. The robot arm should have a relay that has an audible click once the button is engaged. The LEDs on the robot arm should change color. The robot arm should respond to the button press in under 1 second.
5. The robot arm should move in all directions smoothly without interruption.
6. The robot arm relay should have an audible click again. The LED’s on the robot arm return to the ready state color. The robot arm holds its position within 1 second of the button’s release. The robot arm is immovable with the same pressure applied in Step 5.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FHI-55
  ROLE: Verifies

